## Effective-policy audit

A direct non-fetching default built-in audit passed. All 126 policy leaves have valid classification/candidate flags and nonempty source references. Digest:

```text
744104da98b205d73b827d9ecd90e610dbc9d830eb11adc09b31cc034b3a006a
```

Classification counts: active fixed 81, active tunable 25, advisory/unsupported 8, causal invariant 12.

The policy confirms `strategy_basis=CANSLIM-derived`, owner `multi_agent_backtest_loop`, objective `maximize_return_and_minimize_drawdown`, and `optimization_executed_by_this_build=false`. CANSLIM thresholds/weights are active-fixed optimizer candidates, not universal hard constraints. PIT visibility, completed-session facts, next-open/revalidation, and cash/no-leverage are causal invariants. Supported market/regime controls are active tunables; hard-coded behavior-bearing rules are active fixed.

The audit confirmed actual sizing `portfolio_equity * position_risk_pct / stop_loss_pct` and scale tiers `[[0.1, 0.25], [0.15, 0.25], [0.2, 0.25]]`. The seven inert compatibility fields are all advisory/unsupported: `min_rs_score`, `min_canslim_score`, `min_technical_score`, `position_size_pct`, `take_profit_pct`, `scale_out_fraction`, and `min_c_a_growth`. `take_profit_pct=0.41` rejects before data access.

Injected-strategy checks also passed: opaque custom strategies are declared `engine_owned_envelope_only` with unattested internals; a JSON-safe declared identity expands scope only to `engine_owned_envelope_plus_declared_custom_identity`.

